@mfreed7  Wait, I thought XSLT wasn't used by billions? If we could make an extension that doesn't affect other parts of the browser (see the issue I opened in your extension repository about performance), at worst only that rarely-actually-used extension could break, right?

But anyway, thanks for that polyfill and for that extension!
I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of maintenance will be needed for those preferred non-bundled XSLT-support extensions, hopefully they're also open source.
